    "md5": "bfda2accab6f8dc03345796bf8f7d6b2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2072,
    "chunk_text": "The Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n\u027c \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u021d\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u01e6\u01b5\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u01cf \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u024f \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dc3\u0178 \u0db4\u01b4\u0dba\n\n\u0d85\u01af \u026a\u0dd9\u0dc1\u0dc2\n\n\u0d85\u0d82\u0d9a 2152/58 - 2019 \u0dd9\u0daf\u0dc3\u0dd0\u023c\u0db6\u0259 \u0db8\u0dc3 05 \u0dc0\u0dd0\u01e7 \u022f\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dca\u0db4\u01af\u01e6\u0daf\u0dcf - 2019.12.05\n\nNo. 2152/58 \u2013 THURSDAY, DECEMBER 05, 2019\n\nEXTRAORDINARY\n\nYATIYANTHOTA PRADESHIYA SABHA\n\nBy-Law regarding Maintenance of Dangerous and Unpleasant Business\n\nThis is to notify that I, Dhamma Dissanayake, Governor of the Sabaragamuwa Province has approved the By-law regarding maintenance of Dangerous, Unpleasant, Dangerous and Unpleasant business within authoritative area of Yatiyanthota Pradeshiya Sabha, prepared by the Yatiyanthota Pradeshiya Sabha by virtue of powers vested in it under Section 122 read with section 126 of Pradeshiya Sabha Act,, No. 15 of 1987 and passed at its general meeting held on 09.07.2019, by virtue of powers vested under section 123(1) of Pradeshiya Sabha Act, read with Section 2 of Provincial Council (Consequential Provisions) Act,, No. 12 of 1989, and it will be effective within authoritative area of Yatiyanthota Pradeshiya Sabha from the date this notification is published in the Gazette. DHAMMA DISSANAYAKE, Governor, Sabaragamuwa Province. At the Sabaragamuwa Provincial Council, On this 30th day of October, 2019.\n\n(Published by Authority)\n\nPART IV (A) - PROVINCIAL COUNCILS\n\nProvincial Council Notifications\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\n1A PG 4810 - 20 (2019/12)\n\n2 A IV(\u0d85) \u0dd9\u0d9a\u02a3\u0da7\u0dc3 - \u027c \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u021d\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u01e6\u01b5\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u01cf \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u024f \u0d85\u01af \u026a\u0dd9\u0dc1\u0dc2 \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dc3\u0178 \u0db4\u01b4\u0dba - 2019.12.05 PART IV(A) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 05.12.2019\n\nBy-law on Dangerous, Unpleasant, Dangerous and Unpleasant business operated within the area of\n\nauthority of Yatiyanthota Pradeshiya Sabha\n\n1. This By-Law is enacted to regulate, administrate and control businesses which are in the area of the Yatiyanthota PradeshiyaSabha."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_extraordinary_gazettes_2010s",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-05-2019-12-05-2152-58-en",
    "num": "2019-12-05-2152-58-en",
    "date_str": "2019-12-05",
    "description": "Sabaragamuwa  Provincial Council   -  By-Laws of  Ytiyanthota   Pradeshiya  Sabha",
    "url_metadata": "https://documents.gov.lk/view/extra-gazettes/egz_2019.html",
    "lang": "en",
    "url_pdf": "https://documents.gov.lk/view/extra-gazettes/2019/12/2152-58_E.pdf",
    "doc_number": "2152/58",
    "chunk_id": "2019-12-05-2019-12-05-2152-58-en-0001",
    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "7b735473c899606a65256bb37ffe6bef",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1833,
    "chunk_text": "By-law on Dangerous, Unpleasant, Dangerous and Unpleasant business operated within the area of\n\nauthority of Yatiyanthota Pradeshiya Sabha\n\n1. This By-Law is enacted to regulate, administrate and control businesses which are in the area of the Yatiyanthota PradeshiyaSabha.\n\n3.(1) No person shall maintain a business premises in the area of the Yatiyanthota Pradeshiya Sabha, (hereinafter referred to as the premises) unless there is a valid license issued by the Chairman.\n\n3.(2) A person who wishes to obtain a license pursuant to section 3 (1) above shall apply by an application prepared in accordance with the fourth schedule of this by-law.\n\n3.(3) The fee for a license under this by-law shall be lawful by the Sabha, subject to the provisions of the Basic Law, and shall be determined by a resolution of the Sabha.\n\n04.(1) Any person who wishes to commence and maintain a premises which is subject to a permit under section 3(1) above shall have his prior approval of the Chairman under this by-law and otherwise there is no entitlement to apply for a license under section 3(2) of the Act,.\n\n4.(2) A request for prior approval under this section shall be approved by the Chairman on the recommendation of the Public Health Inspector and the Medical Officer of Health.\n\n4.(3) The inspection fee to be charged under the approval of this section may be determined by the Sabha from time to time by the passed resolution.\n\n5. Every person applying for a license under section 3(1) of this by-law must meet the following conditions:\n\n5.(1) Approval under section 4(1) of the by-law when the business is a start-up business.\n\n5.(2) If zoning has been done or industrial zones have been designated, the zoning shall comply with the construction of buildings for Dangerous, Unpleasant and Dangerous and Unpleasant business locations."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_extraordinary_gazettes_2010s",
    "doc_id": "2019-12-05-2019-12-05-2152-58-en",
