    "chunk_text": "15. Everything, including utensils and utensils used in any business or storage under this by-law, shall be thoroughly cleaned.\n\n16. Every Sinhala, Tamil and English copy of this by-law shall be displayed in a publicly visible place in every licensed premises.\n\n18. The President, the Medical Officer of Health, the Public Health Inspector, and any other officer authorized by the Chairman to exercise the authority of these by-laws at any reasonable time, shall give the Licensee all reasonable assistance.\n\n19. It is an offense to maintain premises without a permit under this by-law or to violate any of the provisions of the by-law, and after being convicted by a court of competent jurisdiction for such offense, 122 of the Pradeshiya Sabha Act, No. 15 of 1987 (2) subject to a fine referred to in subsection (2). When a person who has been convicted of an offense continues to violate or violate the offense by a court of competent jurisdiction over the said offense, the Chairman or the Medical Officer of Health or the Public Health Inspector shall issue a written notice of the violation. Each subsequent day the violation continues an additional fine of the said clause shall also be liable.\n\n20. Unless otherwise required in this by-law.\n\n\"Chairman\" shall mean the person holding the office of the Chairman of the Pradeshiya Sabha or performing the functions of that office.\n\n6 A IV(\u0d85) \u0dd9\u0d9a\u02a3\u0da7\u0dc3 - \u027c \u0dbd\u0d82\u0d9a\u0dcf \u021d\u0da2\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf\u01e6\u01b5\u0d9a \u0dc3\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da2\u0dc0\u0dcf\u01cf \u0da2\u0db1\u0dbb\u0da2\u0dd9\u024f \u0d85\u01af \u026a\u0dd9\u0dc1\u0dc2 \u0d9c\u0dd0\u0dc3\u0178 \u0db4\u01b4\u0dba - 2019.12.05 PART IV(A) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 05.12.2019\n\n\"Pradeshiya Sabha\" shall mean Ayagama Pradeshiya Sabha\n\n\u201cMedical Officer of Health\" shall mean the person holding the office of any Medical Officer of Health in the area of the Divisional Council area.\n\n\"Public Health Inspector\" shall mean the person holding the office of any Public Health Inspector in the area of the Pradeshiya Sabha.\n\n\"Authorized officer\" shall mean any officer authorized by the Chairman at the moment,"
