    "chunk_text": "wxl 2154$7 - 2019 foie\u00efn\u00be ui 17 jeks w`.yrejdod - 2019'12'17\n\nNo. 2154/7 \u2013 TUESDAY, DECEMBER 17, 2019\n\nThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\n(Published by Authority)PART III \u2013 LANDS\n\nLand Acquisition Notices\n\nYS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\nEXTRAORDINARY\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nThis Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www. documents.gov.lk\n\nTHE LAND ACQUISITION ACT (CHAPTER 460)\n\nNotice under Section 7\n\nMy Ref. No.: Sri J'pura/LA/77/UDA.\n\nI hereby give notice, under Sub-section (1) of Section 7 of theLand Acquisition Act, No. 28 of 1964, that the Governmentintends to acquire the following lands which are required forthe public purpose:\n\nDescription of the Land or Servitude to be Acquired:\n\nFour Allotments of lands depicted as Lot Nos. 1,2,3, and 4an extent of 0.5635 Hectare in Preliminary Plan No. Co. 9840dated 03.10.2019 prepared by Surveyor General situated at SriJayawardenapura Kotte Municipal Council Limit, GramaNiladari Division of 514C, Obesekarapura, Welikada villagewithin the limits of Sri Jayawardenapura Kotte DivisionalSecretariat Area in the Colombo District, Western Province.\n\n1. Lot No. 1Name of the Land: Rajagiriya Kumbura, Obesekarapurawatta,Assmt. No. 148/B of Arunodaya Mawatha and other;\n\nG 31654- 15 (2019/12)\n\nDescription: Garden, two storied permanent building, twopermanent buildings, part of permanent building, temporarybuilding and part of temporary building; Claimant: Commissionof Land Reforms; Extent: 0.0083 Hectare.\n\n2. Lot No. 02Name of the Land: Not included; Description: Cement drain;Claimant: Commission of Land Reform; Extent: 0.0009Hectare.\n\n3. Lot No. 03Name of the Land: Rajagiriya Kumbura, Obesekarapurawatta, Assmt. No. B/151/1 of Arunodaya Mawatha andothers; Description: Garden, permanent two storied building,12 permanent buildings, 20 temporary buildings, parts of 2permanent buildings and parts of 2 temporary buildings;Claimant: Commission of Land Reforms; Extent: 0.1363 Hectare."
