    "chunk_text": "I fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'12'18PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA -18.12.20191A\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nwxl 2154$10 - 2019 foie\u00efn\u00be ui 18 jeks nodod - 2019'12'18No. 2154/10 - WEDNESDAY, DECEMBER 18, 2019\n\nEXTRAORDINARYThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\nI, hereby declare that out of the powers and functions vested in me in my capacity as the Minister of Sports and YouthAffairs of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka powers and functions specified in the following schedule aredelegated to the State Minister of Sports and Youth Affairs Duminda Dissanayake in terms of provisions of the Article44(5) of the constitution and he has the opportunity of inquiring, mediating and coordinating all functions coming withinthe scope of work of this Ministry.\n\nPART I : SECTION (I) \u2014 GENERAL\n\n1A G 31656 \u2014 417 (12/2019)This Gazette Extraordinary can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\n(Published by Authority)\n\nGovernment Notifications\n\nColumn IDuties and Functions\n\n1. Programmes with a view to launch aNational programmes of meeting theaspiration of the youth.\n\n2. Implementation of youth-centricinternational development cooperationprogrammes.\n\n3. Implementation of unemployed youth-centric skills development programmes.\n\n4. Youth organizations related regulatory anddevelopment activities.\n\nColumn IIDepartments, StatutoryInstitutions & PublicCorporations\n\n1. National Youth Services Council.\n\n2. National Youth Corps.\n\n3. National Youth Awards Authority.\n\n4. National Youths Services Co-operative Limited.\n\n5. National Centre for LeadershipDevelopment.\n\n6. Institute of Smart Sri Lanka.\n\nColumn IIILaws and Ordinance to beImplemented\n\n\u2022 National Youth ServiceCouncil Act, No. 69 of 1979.\n\n\u2022 Youth Corps Act, No. 21 of2002.\n\n\u2022 Children and Young PersonsOrdinance, No. 48 of 1939."
