    "chunk_text": "Towards the reserve area from the bank; Stream/River Stream/River bottom width (Meters) for open stream (Meters) for covered stream (Meters)\n\n< b < 1.2 3.0 0.6 1.2 < b < 3.0 3.0 1.2 3.0 < b < 4.5 3.5 4.5 < b < 6.0 4.0 6.0 < b < 9.0 4.5 b > 9.0 6.5\n\nConditions and orders:-\n\n(a) Unless there is recommendation in writing from the Director of irrigation of the Southern Province Irrigation Department, no construction of buildings, structural work or reclamation work should take place within the stream reservation, declared as a reservation area.\n\n(b) The minimum area of reservation relevant as per the attached list, should be maintained in the \ufb01 eld.\n\n(c) It is necessary obtain the permission of the Provincial Director of Irrigation to build a boundary wall or a fence within thereservation, and such approval for a particular place would be granted subject to signing a \u2018no - compensation\u2019 agreement. In this, the approval will be granted based on the observations made by the District irrigation Engineers on the \ufb01 eld reports (A specimen of the \u2018no-compensation\u2019 agreement is attached as attachement 1).\n\nReservation areas for Reservoirs and Lagoons:-\n\nThe reservation area of a reservoir or lagoon, is generally determined as the wetting area of purview covered by a point 0.5 meters high on the perpendicular line of High Flood Level-HFL. This area however, should not exceed a length of 6.5 meters from the reservoir / lagoon bund. Despite that position however, any construction taking place beyond the said area could be subject to the following conditions."
