    "chunk_text": "The reservation area of a reservoir or lagoon, is generally determined as the wetting area of purview covered by a point 0.5 meters high on the perpendicular line of High Flood Level-HFL. This area however, should not exceed a length of 6.5 meters from the reservoir / lagoon bund. Despite that position however, any construction taking place beyond the said area could be subject to the following conditions.\n\nIV ^w& fldgi \u2013 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h \u2013 2019'12'19P\u0d7a\u0d8b\u0d8d IV (A) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 19.12.2019\n\n3A\n\n(ii) In lands that are developed for sale in the areas in proximity to reservoirs or lagoons, drains and silt traps should be arranged to prevent rainwater from \ufb02 owing into the reservoir or lagoon in keeping with the recommendations of the Director of irrigation. Since such lands could be expected to undergo ground preparation for about an year, to control situations of the \ufb02 ow of muddy water in to the reservoir during the rainy seasons, either a legally valid agreement should be entered in to with the Local Government authorities or a deposit of money could be made with the Provincial Irrigation department, as a means of controlling or compensating such eventuality.\n\n(iii) When developing lands in the proximity of reservation areas relating to streams, reservoirs and lagoons, prior recommendations for such developments should be obtained from the Provincial Director of Irrigation.\n\nSpecial Note:-\n\nIn a situation where there are issues connected to the demarcations of a particular reservation area, action should be taken in keeping with the recommendations obtained from, either the Provincial Director of irriagaiton or from an investigation carried out by a committee appointed by him.\n\n02. The declarations of streams, reservoris, waterways and other aquifers owned by the Southern province Irrigation Department.\n\nAs per attachment No. 02, 03, 04 or 05.\n\n03. Services supplied at a fee."
