    "chunk_text": "4. The request of a Contracting State that has been accepted for collection by the other Contracting State shall befulfilled by this other Contracting State as though such request were related to its own tax.\n\n6. Amounts collected by competent authority of a Contracitng State pursuant to this Article shall be forwarded to thecompetent authority of the other Contracting State. Except where the competent authorities of the ContractingState otherwise agree, the ordinary expenses incurred in providing tax collection assistance shall be borne by therequested Contracting State.\n\n7. Nothing in this Article shall be construed so as to impose on a Contracting State the obligation :\n\n(a) to carry out administrative measures at varinace with the laws and administrative practice of that or of theother Contracting State;\n\n(b) to carry out measures which would be contrary to public policy (ordre public);\n\n(c) to provide assistance if the other Contracting State has not pursued all reasonable measures of collection,available under its laws or administative practice;\n\n(d) to provide assistance in those cases where the administrative burden for that Contracting State is clearlydisproportionate to the benefit to be derived by the other Contracting State.\n\nI fldgi ( ^I& fPoh - YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'12'20PART I : SEC. (I) - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA -20.12.201917A\n\nArticle 28\n\nMEMBERS OF DIPLOMATIC MISSIONS AND CONSULAR POSTS\n\nNothing in this Agreement shall affect the fiscal privileges of members of diplomatic missions or consular posts underthe general rules of international law or under the provisions of special agreements.\n\nArticle 29\n\nENTRY INTO FORCE"
